  "code": "2733",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li>EPO levels are raised in Primary anaemia i.e. iron deficiency anaemia and also in some anaemia of chronic diseases&nbsp;such as arthritis and secondary polycythemia such as due to smoking, pulmonary diseases and cardiac disease.</li>\n<li>EPO levels are decreased in chronic renal failure, anephric individuals, polycythemia vera.</li>\n<li>Erythropoietin levels show diurnal variation. Most consistent results are seen during 7:30 am to 12 noon.<br><br><br></li>\n</ul>",
